---
import Shell from '../../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import DongriaReadingSequence from '../../../components/DongriaReadingSequence.astro';
import guide from '../../../data/dongria-reading-guide.json';
import articles from '../../../data/dongariya.json';
import book from '../../../data/dongariya-book.json';
import reading from '../../../data/dongria-book-reading.json';
import '../../../styles/article-reading.css';
const cover=reading.cover.at(-1)!;
const route=(slug:string)=>`/stories/dongria/${articles.find(a=>a.slug===slug)?.routeSlug || slug}/`;
const escaped=(s:string)=>s.replaceAll('&','&amp;').replaceAll('<','&lt;').replaceAll('>','&gt;').replaceAll('"','&quot;');
const credit=(s:string)=>escaped(s).replace(/\[([^\]]+)\]\((https?:\/\/[^\s)]+)\)/g,'<a href="$2">$1</a>');
const mapLabels=['Rayagada Forest Division working plan, §1.2.2','Niyamgiri field study, surveyed sites','Rayagada Municipality, location','Rayagada District Profile, §2.1'];
---
<Shell title="Dongria Kondh: Life in Niyamgiri — the book" description="Begin with a shawl, then follow the people, food, cloth, learning and songs of Niyamgiri. Read the connected book online or download the illustrated edition." active="explore" related={false} shareImage={{src:cover.src,alt:reading.cover_alt,width:cover.width,height:cover.height}}>
<article class="article-reading dongria-book">
<p><a href="/stories/dongria/">← Dongria Kondh: life in Niyamgiri</a></p>
<header><p class="eyebrow">The book · Read online or take it with you</p><h1>Dongria Kondh:<br/>Life in Niyamgiri</h1><p>By Ahimanikya Satapathy</p>
<div class="book-opening"><figure><img src={cover.src} srcset={reading.cover.map(v=>`${v.src} ${v.width}w`).join(', ')} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 70vw, 300px" width={cover.width} height={cover.height} alt={reading.cover_alt} fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>The cover of the illustrated reading edition.</figcaption></figure><div><p>A shawl bought at a supper club opened questions about the people behind the cloth. The reading led to Site Jakesika’s embroidery, Mukteswar Wadaka’s teaching, seeds kept in circulation and songs remembered across generations.</p><p><a href="#author-note">Begin with the author’s note →</a></p><p><a href={book.file}>Download the illustrated reading edition · PDF</a><br/>{book.pages} pages · {(book.bytes/1000000).toFixed(1)} MB</p></div></div></header>
<nav class="book-contents" aria-label="Book contents"><h2>Read the book online</h2><ol><li><a href="#author-note">A shawl, and the questions it opened</a></li><li><a href="#before-we-begin">Before we begin</a></li><li><a href="#locator">Locating Niyamgiri</a></li><li><a href="#chapters">Twelve connected chapters</a></li><li><a href="#looking-again">Looking again</a></li><li><a href="#glossary">Words in this book</a></li><li><a href="#sources">Footnotes &amp; Sources</a></li></ol></nav>
<section id="author-note"><p class="eyebrow">Author’s note</p><h2>{reading.author_note.title}</h2>{reading.author_note.paragraphs.map((p,i)=><Fragment><p>{p}</p>{i===1&&<figure class="author-story-photo"><img src={reading.author_story_photo.variants.at(-1)!.src} srcset={reading.author_story_photo.variants.map(v=>`${v.src} ${v.width}w`).join(", ")} sizes="(max-width: 464px) calc(100vw - 44px), 420px" width={reading.author_story_photo.variants.at(-1)!.width} height={reading.author_story_photo.variants.at(-1)!.height} alt={reading.author_story_photo.caption} loading="lazy"/><figcaption>{reading.author_story_photo.caption}</figcaption></figure>}</Fragment>)}<p><a href="#before-we-begin">Continue: Before we begin →</a></p></section>
<section id="before-we-begin"><h2>{reading.preface.title}</h2><blockquote><p>{reading.preface.paragraphs[0]}</p><footer>{reading.preface.paragraphs[1]}</footer></blockquote>{reading.preface.paragraphs.slice(2).map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</section>
<section id="locator"><h2>{reading.map.title}</h2><figure><svg viewBox="0 0 680 470" role="img" aria-labelledby="locator-title locator-description"><title id="locator-title">Niyamgiri north of Rayagada town</title><desc id="locator-description">A schematic locator in Odisha. Kalahandi district is labelled northwest of Niyamgiri; Rayagada district is labelled southeast. No boundaries or travel routes are shown.</desc><text x="55" y="45" class="map-state">Odisha, India</text><path d="M605 95V45m-10 12 10-12 10 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><text x="599" y="30">N</text><text x="55" y="125">Kalahandi district</text><text x="405" y="270">Rayagada district</text><text x="320" y="180" text-anchor="middle" class="map-region">Niyamgiri hills</text><text x="320" y="205" text-anchor="middle" class="map-detail">approximate regional position</text><circle cx="334" cy="360" r="5"/><text x="349" y="366">Rayagada town</text></svg><figcaption>{reading.map.display_caption}</figcaption></figure><p>Niyamgiri is shown as an approximate regional position north of Rayagada town. The locator does not mark a summit, a village or a route.</p></section>
<section id="chapters"><h2>Twelve connected chapters</h2><p>{guide.section_intro}</p><DongriaReadingSequence headingLevel={3}/></section>
<section id="looking-again"><h2>{reading.closing.title}</h2>{reading.closing.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</section>
<section id="glossary"><h2>Words in this book</h2><p>These short definitions explain how the terms are used in this book. Personal and place-name spellings follow the cited accounts and may vary.</p><dl>{reading.glossary.map(entry=><div><dt>{entry.term}</dt><dd>{entry.definition} <a href={route(entry.chapter_slug)}>Read the chapter</a>.</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
<section id="author"><h2>About the author</h2><figure class="author"><img src={reading.author_portrait.at(-1)!.src} width={reading.author_portrait.at(-1)!.width} height={reading.author_portrait.at(-1)!.height} alt="Ahimanikya Satapathy" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Ahimanikya Satapathy</figcaption></figure><p>{reading.author_bio}</p></section>
<section id="sources"><h2>Footnotes &amp; Sources</h2><h3>The chapters</h3><p>The twelve chapters retain their fuller online source notes. The PDF brings the same sources together in a compact list.</p><ul>{articles.map(a=><li><a href={route(a.slug)+'#footnote-label'}>{a.title}: source notes</a></li>)}</ul><h3>Author’s note photograph</h3><p>{reading.author_story_photo.credit}</p><h3>Before we begin</h3><p><a href="https://grain.org/en/article/743-endangered-tribals-up-against-the-terror-of-vedanta">Living Farms, GRAIN, 26 July 2009</a>; translator unnamed.</p><h3>Locator</h3><ul>{reading.map.sources.map((s,i)=><li><a href={s.url}>{mapLabels[i]}</a>.</li>)}</ul><h3>Glossary</h3><ul>{reading.glossary.map(e=><li>{e.term}: <a href={e.source_url}>{e.source_title || 'source'}</a>.</li>)}</ul><h3>Pictures in the book</h3><p>Front cover photograph: {reading.cover_credit.creator}. <a href={reading.cover_credit.source_url}>Source</a>. <a href={reading.cover_credit.licence_url}>{reading.cover_credit.licence}</a>. The preview reproduces the published cover.</p>{reading.chapter_credits.map(c=><p><strong>{c.title}.</strong> <Fragment set:html={credit(c.text)}/></p>)}{reading.additional_photographs.map(p=><p>{p.caption} Photograph: {p.creator}. <a href={p.source_url}>Source</a>. <a href={p.licence_url}>{p.licence}</a>. Resized; composition unchanged.</p>)}<p>Interpretive stitch-band drawing: Project Odisha. Technique reference: Kanak Rajadhyaksha, <a href="https://www.sahapedia.org/kapdagondas-motifs-and-technique">Kapdagondas: Motifs and Technique</a>, Sahapedia. Hairpin drawing: interpretive adaptation by Project Odisha from a <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dangaria_accessory_detail_01.jpg">photograph by Pillai Sree Vidya</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>; adaptation under the same licence. Drawings simplify details. Author portrait: supplied by Ahimanikya Satapathy.</p></section>
<p><a href={book.file}>Download the illustrated reading edition · {book.pages} pages · PDF</a></p>
</article></Shell>
<style>
.dongria-book{max-width:804px;padding-inline:32px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.dongria-book section{margin-block:3rem}.dongria-book img{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto}.book-opening{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.2fr);gap:2rem;align-items:center}.book-opening figure{margin:0}.book-opening img{width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5}.book-opening figcaption{font-size:.9rem;margin-top:.75rem}.book-contents{border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding-block:1rem;margin-block:3rem}.book-contents ol,.chapter-list{padding-left:1.5rem}.book-contents li,.chapter-list li{margin-block:.6rem}.dongria-book dl>div{margin-block:1.5rem}.dongria-book dt{font-weight:700}.dongria-book dd{margin:.3rem 0}.dongria-book svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:68/47;color:var(--sea)}.dongria-book svg text{fill:currentColor;font-size:20px}.dongria-book svg .map-state{font-size:24px}.dongria-book svg .map-region{fill:var(--earth);font-size:28px}.dongria-book svg .map-detail{font-size:16px}.author{max-width:220px}.author-story-photo{max-width:420px;margin-inline:auto!important}.author-story-photo img{aspect-ratio:1365/2048}.dongria-book [id]{scroll-margin-top:2rem}#sources{font-size:.95rem}blockquote footer{font-size:1rem}a{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:640px){.dongria-book{padding-inline:22px}.book-opening{grid-template-columns:1fr}.book-opening figure{max-width:280px;margin-inline:auto}}
</style>
